What you’ll do &nbsp;

The Client Coordinator provides a variety of professional support services to Client Service teams in the areas of project

management, client liaison, internal team coordination and documentation.

Job Responsibilities

Works with Client Services colleagues for everyday project management of client work

• Controls basic project requirements, assists in managing timelines and resources accordingly, writing timely meeting&nbsp;minutes, ensuring that the project team know the project status and have everything they need

• Helps ensure all correspondence, materials, presentations, proposals seen by clients are error-free, and reflective of&nbsp;the Landor brand

• Contributing to the preparation of cost estimates that define the scope of work, preparing timelines, alongside&nbsp;scrutinizing budgets.

• Learning how to budget, forecast, invoice, resource and maintain tight management of ongoing project budgets

• Assisting the Landor team with diary management, room bookings, meeting logistics and travel itineraries or travel&nbsp;arrangements and bookings

• Helps to update regular client status reports, resourcing requests and invoicing

• Building a good understanding of the client and their business

• Demonstrates the ability to accurately interpret client briefs, thinking both strategically and creatively

• Building sound judgment of creative or strategic work, identifying where work is considered off brief

• Supports the creative and production process, including briefing, amends and delivery

  &nbsp;

What you’ll need &nbsp;

&nbsp;

• Project management skills - working to deadlines, working flexibly and within a budget

• Interested in understanding branding, Landor, new information and new ideas

• Comfortable managing internal stakeholders

• Good organization and time keeping skills

&nbsp;

